2026-09-27T04:47:38.1307052Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1307256Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1307528Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1307789Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1307874Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1308074Z ================
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1308194Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1308341Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1308691Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1308898Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1309007Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1309270Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1309435Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1309570Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1309985Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1310328Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1310966Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1311483Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1311588Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1312029Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1312549Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1313104Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1313449Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1313880Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1313970Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1314157Z ========
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1314270Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1315499Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1316786Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1316998Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1317451Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1317894Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1383254Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1383956Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1384486Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1384792Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1385300Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1385577Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1385739Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1386793Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1388094Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1388726Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1389589Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:47:38.1389801Z 
